# S_UNDEF unknown=fail / unknown=warning (D-0283 item 1).  Diff of the engine-core hunk in src/pl-wam.jl.
# Code SHA on this stack: 25e9b29 (old branch: a9015c5).  Rows: sf37 (unknown=fail, an undefined call fails)
# and sf90 (unknown=warning, the existence_error warning is printed) in test/core_lang/test_set_flag_swipl.jl;
# sf90's call reads the printed message through a white-box read (ad26fbd).
# (c) the @goto deep_backtrack target against pl-vmi.c S_UNDEF, swipl-devel cbf4e1896275:
#   src/pl-vmi.c:3369  VMI(S_UNDEF ...)       switch( getUnknownModule(DEF->module) )
#   src/pl-vmi.c:3418-3422  case UNKNOWN_FAIL: default: [debugging newChoice] FRAME_FAILED;
#   src/pl-wam.c:2528  #define FRAME_FAILED  GO(deep_backtrack, PL_TRACE_ACTION_NONE)
# so the fail path is deep_backtrack, as `@goto deep_backtrack` (src/pl-wam.jl, same label every FRAME_FAILED
# in this file uses, e.g. pl-wam.jl:4465, 4538).  UNKNOWN_WARNING prints, takes `if (exception_term) THROW_EXCEPTION`
# (vmi:3414-3415), and FALLS THROUGH to the fail path (pl-vmi.c has no break): the Julia `elseif` branch does the same.
# The line numbers in the source comment (3335-3339, 2465) are those of the older bae881a2 checkout.
