    FIXED: pl-wam.jl S_UNDEF unknown=fail/warning branches (pl-vmi.c S_UNDEF)
    
    S_UNDEF asserted the module's unknown flag was UNKNOWN_ERROR; set_prolog_flag(unknown, ...)
    (F1b) makes the other two reachable. Ported as pl-vmi.c: the error branch as it was; the
    warning branch prints error(existence_error(procedure, PI), _) as a warning through
    printMessage, throws if that raised, and falls through; the fail branch (and default) is
    FRAME_FAILED. The debugger's CHP_DEBUG choice point of the fail branch is left out (no debugger).
    ENGINE CORE (Tier 1) edit by a Sonnet agent: flagged for the audit's review.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

